Add the ryzen_smu SMU command driver as an in-tree module.

Imports drv.c/smu.c/smu.h from amkillam/ryzen_smu (GPL-2.0, based on
leogx9r/ryzen_smu) into drivers/misc/ryzen_smu/ and wires a new
tristate CONFIG_RYZEN_SMU into drivers/misc. The driver binds to the
MP1/RSMU/HSMP mailbox PCI functions and exposes SMU service commands
plus the Renoir power-monitor table under /sys/kernel/ryzen_smu_drv/.

Used for dynamic power management on Zen 2 systems whose firmware does
not expose CPPC (_CPC): STAPM and related limits can be adjusted at
runtime instead of relying on amd_pstate. The module is built but not
auto-loaded; enabling it is an explicit choice.

Upstream: https://github.com/amkillam/ryzen_smu @ d298366

